{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01PNUFzkJXf94xNHosEBB3hj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q8: How handle hallucination when no information is found in context?**\n\nThe answer note builds out a **four-layer defense-in-depth stack**:\n\n1. **Retrieval confidence gate** — compute cosine similarity (or cross-encoder score) before calling the LLM; if max similarity < θ (≈0.70), return a canned abstention response immediately — no LLM call, no hallucination risk, saves inference cost\n2. **Grounding prompt + T=0** — explicit system instruction: \"Answer ONLY from context; if insufficient, say exactly: 'I don't have enough information'\" with temperature=0 for determinism\n3. **Post-generation faithfulness gate** — RAGAS faithfulness (decompose claims → verify entailment) or DeBERTa NLI; if score < 0.8, swap answer for abstention message\n4. **Production monitoring** — track abstention rate (>30% = threshold too strict; <2% = model answering out-of-scope) and hallucination rate on golden datasets separately\n\nKey pitfall flagged: saying \"just add 'if you don't know, say so' to the prompt\" is wrong — LLMs override soft instructions when context is partially relevant; you need the retrieval gate *before* generation."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":348,"cache_read_input_tokens":62512,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":348,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1073847b-04cf-409b-9f3c-b605de693a97","uuid":"8f99414a-0218-4288-873b-7d3920a3c608"}
